Dear all,

short summary: it still doesn't work.

long summary:

 some additional info: the ethernet card is a "KZPCM PCI-to-Dual
 Channel UltraSCSI and 10/100MB Ethernet Hosts Adapter", capable of
 full- and half-duplex at 10 and 100 Mbit. It reports as DE500-AA
 using 'show config'. It worked before with a Lantronix LSW8F switch
 fine when setting ewa0_mode to 'FastFD'.

 - several people suggested to try different configurations in the
   switch. Since this is a very basic mini switch it can't be
   configured.

 - most people mentioned that setting the card to 'Auto-Negotiate' at
   the SRM prompt might not be a good idea. However, the setting in
   SRM was Fast or FastFD anyway.

 - several suggested using the 'lan_config' or 'ifconfig' utility
   after botting: no luck. Leaving ewa0_mode at 'Twisted-Pair' and the
   using

     lan_config -i tu0 -s 100 -a 0 -m utp
     lan_config -i tu0 -s 200 -a 0 -m utp

   made the LED on the network disappear. Whic is not suprising since
   setting ewa0_mode to anything else but 'TWISTED-PAIR' or 'FULL
   DUPLEX TWISTE PAIR' didn't work. So to me there seems to be some
   fundamental hardware problem between the switch and the Ethernet
   card.

Solution: using a long cable and plug the ES40 into a Bay Networks
BayStack 350T - works at 100Mb half-duplex.


