way i could create the /etc/fdmns directory, and because of this, i =
didn't even try.&nbsp; stupid me.</FONT></P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#0000FF" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">for some easy steps =
on creating the /etc/fdmns directory, Nix wrote:</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#000080" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial"># (cd /dev ; =
./MAKEDEV rz0)</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#000080" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial"># mkdir -p =
/etc/fdmns/root_domain ; cd /etc/fdmns; mkdir usr_domain</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#000080" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial"># (cd root_domain ; =
ln -s /dev/rz0a)</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#000080" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial"># (cd usr_domain ; =
ln -s /dev/rz0g)</FONT>
<BR><FONT COLOR=3D"#000080" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial"># mount -t advfs =
root_domain#root /mnt</FONT>
</P>

<P><FONT COLOR=3D"#000080" SIZE=3D2 FACE=3D"Arial">and of course after =
these links and directories are created, mounting is easy.</FONT>
</P>

