The original question is below.  Thanks to aad@lovecraft.talltree.net,
Kevin Dea, Marie-Claude Vialatte and especially Maarten Litmaath for
lots of good ideas about what to look for but the big cigar goes
to Bob Vickers who supplied this answer:

> I have seen something similar. What was strangest was that like you said
> it only seemed to affect one or two users. Anyway I searched the web and
> found a suggestion to set the environment variable
>   MOZILLA_NO_ASYNC_DNS=true
> before calling netscape. This stops netscape starting up a separate
> 'helper' process to do DNS and it seemed to solve the problem. Don't ask
> me why!

That solved it.  I don't know why either and I don't have time
to investigate further.


Ian

