Hi,

Thanks go to George Gallen, Calvin Coghlan and especially to Derk Tegeler.
The procedure went thus: install obsolete commands to get bootpd onto the 
5.0A system, edit inetd.conf to include the lines

tftp   dgram   udp     wait    root     /usr/sbin/tftpd    tftpd  -d -r \
/tftpboot /tftpboot
bootps dgram   udp     wait    root     /usr/sbin/bootpd        bootpd

and edit the /etc/bootptab tab file  to include the necessary load images,
MAC address data etc.

Note that for some reason joind which is supplied as standard with 5.0A in 
place of bootpd didn't seem to behave properly. I'll look into this some 
more since I expect the errors are down to me rather than the software.


Cheers


Joe


