Subject: Summary: Multipathing in Tru64 Unix.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=98517304909525

Thanks to both Mr.Alen (alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com ) and Dr.Thomas 
(Dr.Thomas.Blinn@Compaq.com)

Here is the summary.

Mr.Alan's

Multipathing is handled in the SCSI driver.
Unless explicit path selection was a required feature for the first release, 
it may be sometime for a API interface that allows path selection is 
available, if ever.

Dr.Thomas's

Not supported prior to V5.0, generally will not work correctly in V4.x.

There are no APIs.  There is no actual multipathing for storage for 
performance, all I/O is done through one path (to a given device) as long as 
the path works.

Once again thanks,

vsp.

