Dear alpha friends,

About HSZ firmware the answer is that:

	If you have the subscription service for ACS (the name of
	the HSZ operating system), you should have gotten it when
	it came out.  If you didn't, call your local Compaq Service
	center and they should be able to take care of it.  If you
	don't have the subscription service, you'll probably have
	to buy the newer version.  Double check with the service
	center anyway.


About /vmuix CDSL the answer is that I don't need to worry since before
	creating the cluster (my situation) vmunix is located in the
        usual / directory. Creating the cluster creates the CDSL
	/cluster/members/{memb}/boot_partition
	and vmunix is placed overthere. ONLY Then /vmunix will be a link
        to /cluster/members/{memb}/boot_partition/vmunix.

Special thanks to:
	Robert Sandford <sandforr@ohio.edu>
	Jim Fitzmaurice <jpfitz@fnal.gov>
	alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com


