Thanks to all who responded. 

I was trying to setup the DECserver standalone and even rebooting didn't
work properly. After that I connected the thing in our network and added the
following line to the bootptab-file:

DS04:   tc=DS.default:  ha=0000F8EF95BF:  ip=101.10.1.91:      bf=MNENG2:
sm=255.255.255.0: 

I had put a terminal on port 1 and while putting on the 90M I pushed the
reboot button for 10 seconds. This seemed to be the way and now I can setup
everything through the terminal.

Best regards,

Roland



