From: "Dr. Thomas.Blinn@Compaq.com" <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com>

I believe ALL of the DS10 motherboards have the IDE controller chip and
a bulkhead connector that can take two cables (most of the IDE chips are
dual channel), so you could in principle support up to four IDE/ATAPI
drives in the box.  As to whether you can physically mount an IDE drive
or whether there is a suitable cable (not too long) available to connect
the drive to the bulkhead/motherboard, I can't say.  If your handbook for
the system doesn't make this clear, then you probably need to purchase
some more hardware documentation; a service manual would probably have
the details.  Whether this stuff is available on the AlphaServer part of
Compaq's external web pages, I simply don't know, but it's a good place
to start.

